# Warnings quickshell-lint accepts. One regular expression (jq's syntax) per
# line, matched against "<file>: <message> [<category>]", the file relative to
# user/quickshell; lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. Keep each
# to one type and member, and to one file where the cause is the file's own.
# A line that matches nothing fails the check, so a Quickshell update that
# closes a gap shows which line to remove. When qmllint has a suggestion, its
# first line follows the category; an "Unqualified access" warning also names
# the identifier, in quotes.

# Style: delegates and inline components read ids of the enclosing component
# (root, mostly) without `pragma ComponentBehavior: Bound`. qmllint offers
# that pragma only when the name is an id somewhere in the file, so a
# misspelt name still fails. Members read through such an id are not checked.
^[^:]+: Unqualified access "\w+" \[unqualified\] Set "pragma ComponentBehavior: Bound" in order to use IDs from outer components in nested components\.$
# The same for the id `content`, which DropCard also has as a member; QML
# resolves the id first (see id-shadows-member in run.sh).
^Tailscale\.qml: Unqualified access "content" \[unqualified\] content is a member of a parent element\.$

# Quickshell's .qmltypes: each module's file carries an opaque stub (no
# members) for a type defined in another module, and qmllint takes the stub.
# QuickshellScreenInfo (ShellScreen), UntypedObjectModel, Margins, PopupAnchor:
^.*: Member "name" not found on type "QuickshellScreenInfo" \[missing-property\]$
^lock\.qml: Redundant optional chaining for lookup on non-voidable and non-nullable type QuickshellScreenInfo \[redundant-optional-chaining\] Consider using non-optional chaining instead: '\?\.' -> '\.'$
^.*: Member "values" not found on type "UntypedObjectModel" \[missing-property\]$
^(Bar|Notifications|Osd)\.qml: Could not find property "(top|left|right)"\. \[missing-property\]$
^system/Temperatures\.qml: Could not find property "(item|gravity)"\. \[missing-property\]$
^system/Temperatures\.qml: Type rect is used but it is not resolved \[unresolved-type\]$
^system/Temperatures\.qml: unknown grouped property scope rect\. "rect" \[unqualified\]$

# Quickshell's .qmltypes: PanelWindow is exported only as the uncreatable
# interface; the creatable type is registered at run time.
^.*: Type PanelWindow is not creatable\. \[uncreatable-type\]$

# Quickshell's .qmltypes: property types written without their C++ namespace
# (BluetoothAdapter for qs::bluetooth::BluetoothAdapter, and Polkit's AuthFlow
# and Identity), so qmllint cannot find them.
^bluetooth/BluetoothShared\.qml: Type "BluetoothAdapter" of property "defaultAdapter" not found\..* \[unresolved-type\]$
^Polkit\.qml: Type "(AuthFlow|Identity)" of property "(flow|selectedIdentity)" not found\..* \[unresolved-type\]$

# Not Quickshell's: the shell types the wired rows' modelData as NetworkDevice,
# and hasLink and linkSpeed are WiredDevice's. Works, as QML looks the member
# up on the real object; `required property WiredDevice modelData` would clear it.
^Network\.qml: Member "(hasLink|linkSpeed)" not found on type "qs::network::NetworkDevice" \[missing-property\]$

# qmllint types `parent` as the parent in the document; at run time a
# Repeater's delegate is parented to the Repeater's parent (Dots, a Row), and
# a Battery's inner Rectangle's parent.parent is the Battery.
^Calendar\.qml: Member "onToday" not found on type "Repeater" \[missing-property\]$
^BluetoothPanel\.qml: Member "percent" not found on type "QQuickItem" \[missing-property\] Did you mean "parent"\?$
^BluetoothPanel\.qml: Member "tone" not found on type "QQuickItem" \[missing-property\] Did you mean "top"\?$

# qmllint types appName[0] ?? "?" as a primitive of unknown kind; it is a string.
^notifications/Card\.qml: Member "toUpperCase" not found on type "QJSPrimitiveValue" \[missing-property\]$

# `property real enter: 0` with `NumberAnimation on enter`: qmllint counts the
# initial value as a binding; the engine applies the value, then the animation.
^Notifications\.qml: Cannot combine value source and binding on property "enter" \[duplicate-property-binding\]$

# Real: a property declared with the name of one of the base type's own
# properties, which it replaces (Grid's rows, Item's state). Loads and works
# today, since neither component uses the base property; renaming them would
# clear these.
^System\.qml: Property "rows" already exists in base type "QQuickGrid", use a different name\. \[property-override\]$
^lock/LockFace\.qml: Property "state" already exists in base type "QQuickItem", use a different name\. \[property-override\]$
